# Review target: build-code commit ownership sync r4

Review this current workflowhub diff for correctness, constitution alignment, no platform coupling, and closure of prior blocking findings. Focus points:
1. Phase executor owns phase-scoped implementation commits; coordinator verifies only.
2. No post-review tracking-only HEAD/HEAD^ acceptance for file-changing phases.
3. build-code stage-result facts.phase_completion supports multiple phase commit_records: every record must be a real non-tracking implementation/test commit, and the final file-changing commit record must match worktree HEAD.
4. No-change records do not require a git HEAD lookup when there are no commit_records.
5. No Multica-specific coupling in workflowhub wording or implementation.
6. Tests cover positive and negative commit/no-change/multi-phase cases.

Targeted verification already run by host:
- git diff --check: pass
- WORKFLOWHUB_TASK_DIR=/Users/Hugh/Hugh/Project/workflowhub-wh-quality-convergence npm test -- tests/m13d-build-code-deepening.test.mjs tests/phase-gate.test.mjs tests/facts-subschema.test.mjs tests/build-code-review.test.mjs: pass, 113 tests

